  "limitations": "Spherical approximation (Chamberlain and Duquette 2007) on a sphere of radius 6378137 m: typically within a few tenths of a percent of ellipsoidal GIS areas, not survey or cadastral quality. Holes are subtracted by absolute value; self-intersecting rings and overlapping MultiPolygon parts are not detected. Input must fit 64 KB, so very detailed boundaries need simplifying first (for example with M021). Orientation sign: positive means clockwise.",
  "port_notes": "Line-by-line port of geometry, polygonArea, ringArea, rad and isClosed from index.js at the pinned commit, including the implicit closing of unclosed rings and the same summation order. The ring operation exposes upstream ring() with signed output. Inputs are structure-checked (positions [lon, lat] within range) instead of silently returning undefined for unknown types.",
